data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:15:08.769527+00:00", "content": "**Blast-radius trace from `p1` (3 hops) \u2014 all devices currently **up** (interface_ifOperStatus=1) with no interface errors/discards on core links** [topo:p1].\n\n---\n\n### Hop 1 \u2014 Direct neighbors (7 core/aggregation routers)\n| Device | Role hint | Key health |\n|--------|-----------|------------|\n| `p13`  | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=107 [topo:p13] |\n| `p2`   | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=107 [topo:p2] |\n| `p21`  | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=107 [topo:p21] |\n| `p3`   | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=108 [topo:p3] |\n| `p4`   | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=108 [topo:p4] |\n| `p5`   | Core      | Clean interfaces, MPLS LSPs=107 [topo:p5] |\n\n---\n\n### Hop 2 \u2014 Second ring (16 devices)\nCore/aggregation: `p14` `p15` `p16` `p17` `p22` `p23` `p24` `p6` `p7` `p8` `p9` \u2014 all interfaces clean, MPLS LSPs 107-108.  \nEdge PEs: `pe1` `pe2` \u2014 BGP peers established (11 each), LDP sessions up (5), MPLS LSPs=114 [topo:pe1][topo:pe2].\n\n---\n\n### Hop 3 \u2014 **Branch / edge layer (22 devices)**\n**SD-WAN branch CEs (4)** \u2014 *these are the \u201caffected branches\u201d if `p1` fails*:\n| Branch | Latency (ms) | Jitter (ms) | Loss % | Tunnel active |\n|--------|--------------|-------------|--------|---------------|\n| `ce_branch1`   | 29.2  | 21.9 | 0.067 | yes [topo:ce_branch1] |\n| `ce_branch13`  | 58.8  | 37.8 | 0.116 | yes [topo:ce_branch13] |\n| `ce_branch14`  | 86.3  | 36.7 | 0.128 | yes [topo:ce_branch14] |\n| `ce_branch2`   | 66.7  | 43.6 | 0.103 | yes [topo:ce_branch2] |\n\n**Hub CEs (2)** \u2014 high throughput, clean: `ce_hub1` (4.5 GiB in / 4.3 GiB out) [topo:ce_hub1], `ce_hub2` (4.5 GiB in / 4.3 GiB out) [topo:ce_hub2].\n\n**Deeper core/PEs (16)** \u2014 `p10` `p11` `p12` `p18` `p19` `p20` `pe3` `pe4` `pe7` `pe8` `pe11` `pe12` \u2014 all interfaces up, MPLS/BGP healthy.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n- **Total blast radius (\u2264 3 hops): 46 devices**.\n- **Directly impacted branches if `p1` goes down: 4 SD-WAN CEs** (`ce_branch1`, `ce_branch13`, `ce_branch14`, `ce_branch2`) plus 2 hub CEs.\n- No current alarms; all links operational. If you need trend data (latency/jitter/loss over time) on the branch tunnels, I can pull ranged metrics for any of the four `ce_branch*` devices."}

